administrative data? <source>Health Policy</source><year>2003</year>;<volume>65</volume>:<fpage>101</fpage>-7.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12849909</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ref17"><label>17</label><citation citation-type="journal">Polancich S, Restrepo E, Prosser J. Cautious use of administrative data for decubitus ulcer outcome reporting. <source>Am J Med Qual</source><year>2006</year>;<volume>21</volume>:<fpage>262</fpage>-8.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16849783</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ref18"><label>18</label><citation citation-type="other">Department of Health. <source>High quality care for all: NHS next stage review final report</source> London: DH, <year>2008</year> <ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.dh.gov.uk/en/Publicationsandstatistics/Publications/PublicationsPolicyAndGuidance/DH_085825">www.dh.gov.uk/en/Publicationsandstatistics/Publications/PublicationsPolicyAndGuidance/DH_085825</ext-link></citation></ref></ref-list><notes notes-type="citation-text"><p><bold>Cite this as: </bold><italic>BMJ</italic> 2008;337:a1702</p></notes></back></article>